<title>USA: Wells puts merger-related cuts at 10,800.</title>
<headline>Wells puts merger-related cuts at 10,800.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wells Fargo and Co said a total of 10,800 positions will be eliminated by the third quarter of 1997 following its April 1996 merger with First Interstate Bancorp, up from previous forecasts of 9,000.</p>
<p>Wells in a Securities Exchange Commission filing back in April projected 7,200 layoffs by the end of 1996.  But company officials at the time said job cuts would approach 9,000.</p>
<p>In a recent U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission filing, Wells said 3,600 jobs would be cut by the third quarter of 1997 in addition to 7,200 forecast for 1996, bringing the total to 10,800.</p>
<p>&quot;Wells expects to have less than 35,000 people by the end of the third quarter,&quot; a spokeswoman said.</p>
</text>
